# Aura Omega 2.1.0 — DEVELOPMENT CANDIDATE

This is a personal continuation of Aura, updated primarily to keep using the
skin on **Kodi 21.3 Omega**. Its implementation and visual appearance are retained.
Original project: [jurialmunkey/skin.aura](https://github.com/jurialmunkey/skin.aura).
This fork: [kcook98765/skin.aura](https://github.com/kcook98765/skin.aura).
The add-on identity remains `skin.aura`.

**2.1.0 is a development candidate, not an officially validated release.** The
target skin GUI API is **5.17.0**. Static checks are not proof of complete Kodi
functionality; populated-library widgets, playback, full PVR behavior and
Backup/Restore acceptance remain incomplete. This notice/documentation update
does not add skin features, replace assets or establish new runtime acceptance.
See [test status and retained checker findings](docs/TESTING.md).

**Known third-party redistribution restrictions remain unresolved.** Read
[THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt](THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt), included with the skin package.
Attribution and disclosure do not grant missing permissions. Publishing source
and distributing a ZIP both redistribute assets; personal use and candidate
status do not clear those restrictions. No broad asset reconstruction or
replacement is part of this continuation's current preparation scope.

## Branch policy

The layout is prepared locally, not yet published:

| Branch | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `main` | Omega 2.1.0 development candidate |
| `matrix` | Exact historical commit `203aba5117f185a34fef773134d3cf955cbf2c7a` |
| `master` | Existing historical branch, unchanged |
| `Nexus` | Existing Nexus branch, unchanged, including its capitalization |

Historical tags remain unchanged. No history rewrite, old-version support
guarantee or automatic Kodi update is implied. See the bounded
[publication proposal](docs/PUBLICATION.md).

## Dependencies and migration

Use the official Kodi Add-on repository for the declared dependencies and their
transitive requirements. Let Kodi resolve versions appropriate to Omega; do not
follow the former manual GitHub ZIP chain or beta-repository setup. An offline
index audit checks declarations, not actual installation or availability.

Online metadata enrichment is optional and **off by default**. Stored library
metadata is the baseline; extra ratings, awards and artwork depend on provider
coverage and may be unavailable. This guide requires no credentials or account
setup. Enrichment being off does not make every installed dependency network-free.

Existing widgets pointing at removed Skin Helper providers need **manual source
reselection** in the menu/widget editor. Saved shortcuts are not automatically
translated. Review affected widgets individually; do not reset a working profile
to force migration. The airing calendar is not a replacement with identical
behaviour for the old Next Aired guide.

## Bounded testing and recovery

Test only in a disposable Kodi profile with synthetic data and a recoverable
configuration. Before switching skins, keep **Estuary** available; use
**Settings → Interface → Skin → Estuary** to roll back. Switching skins does not
restore changed widgets, add-on data or other settings.

The Backup add-on (`script.xbmcbackup`) must be configured before use: select a
destination, enable **Add-on Data**, include custom asset folders and verify a
restore in the disposable profile. Installing Backup alone creates no backup.
Old Skin Helper backup archives are not supported. Keep backups and saved
settings out of the source tree and public reports.

- [Development and Git policy](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md)
- [Packaging and current builder limits](docs/PACKAGING.md)
- [Static checks and future runtime acceptance](docs/TESTING.md)

These development links refer to the source checkout; `docs/` is deliberately
excluded from the installable skin ZIP. The root third-party notice and existing
license files are included. The five legacy screenshots remain 1366x768 and
fail official repository dimensions; no images were replaced to mask that finding.

